#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "332b1d25-852f-51ad-9a38-62b562ae247f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12522" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(\\pi,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}e^{y}\\cos x & e^{y}\\sin x\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ x_{n}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $\\begin{bmatrix}e^{y}\\cos x & e^{y}\\sin x\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = e^y\\cos x, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} =e^y\\sin x\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(e^{y}\\cos x) =-e^{y}\\sin x & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y}|= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(e^{y}\\sin x) = e^{y}\\cos x \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{y}\\cos x) = e^{y}\\cos x & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{y}\\sin x) = e^{y}\\sin x\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{″}(x, y) &= \\begin{bmatrix}-e^{y}\\sin x & e^{y}\\cos x \\\\ e^{y}\\cos x & e^{y}\\sin x\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\pi,0)$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156930 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523" :question/problem "Given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln y & \\frac{x}{y}\\end{bmatrix}$\nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ x_{n}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det \\left(\\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\right)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln y & \\frac{x}{y}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\ln y, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac xy\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln y) = 0 & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y}|= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}) = \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln y) = \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}) =-\\frac{x}{y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{″}(x, y) &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\nf^{″}(0, 1) = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1) = 0 \\cdot 0 - 1\\cdot 1 = -1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156931 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y) = x^2 e^y$." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ x_{n}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{1}∂x_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{2}∂x_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{1}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}∂x_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x, y) &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}e^{y}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2}e^{y})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2xe^{y} & x^{2}e^{y}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x^{2}} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xe^{y}) = 2e^{y} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y}|= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}e^{y}) = 2xe^{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y∂x}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xe^{y}) = 2xe^{y} & \\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂y^{2}}|= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2}e^{y}) = x^{2}e^{y}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{″}(x, y) &= \\begin{bmatrix}2e^{y} & 2xe^{y} \\\\ 2xe^{y} & x^{2}e^{y}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at\n\n$$\n\\left(1,0\\right)\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\nf^{″}(1, 0) = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871283d2-1f9f-53d5-a229-b02b6a59bee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153402} {:answer/id #uuid "9176a86f-7b1f-5dff-adea-fbfff8ce6aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153403} {:answer/id #uuid "c90476f1-09e0-5ef7-91ae-e5822686aaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153404} {:answer/id #uuid "fb03cb9c-b8af-518f-ae3f-6a83142bec0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153405} {:answer/id #uuid "2f28fe91-990f-5a32-b4fc-2e24861f3c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb03cb9c-b8af-518f-ae3f-6a83142bec0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153405} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b7b11e-e967-5e86-b1e5-589356b1084d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153401}] :question/id #uuid "3b064463-cab9-5bec-b4bd-67252dafbaa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-102477" :question/problem "Find $f^{″}(1, 2)$ for the function $f(x, y)$ given that\n\n$f^{′}(x, y) = \\begin{bmatrix}y - 2xy & x - x^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae64ecf2-f100-5ee1-bf22-d62f17c06d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155627} {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155628} {:answer/id #uuid "30a4bd7f-a653-586c-8d6c-48bbd5f3eadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + x \\\\ \\cos y + x & \\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155629} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54a19a-e583-584b-a065-7c3d2342cae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & x\\cos y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155630} {:answer/id #uuid "7613ab91-83d0-595d-baf0-b61833c485f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155628} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f160e6d-8669-5f1d-a718-6927812f7f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155626}] :question/id #uuid "1fc495d4-08fa-5ada-9f41-a42761e42726" :question/math-academy-id "q-80939" :question/problem "Find $f^{″}(x, y)$ for the function $f(x, y) = x\\sin y + xy$."}]}
